{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1533550-help-with-alternative-setting","id":1533550,"title":"help with alternative setting","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-04-03T20:22:46-07:00","id":1533550,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon4.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> help with alternative setting","content":"Hello, this is my first publication and English is not my native language so if you see any errors that is why.<br /> <br /> I am planning a 3e exalted campaign together with my cousin but we were not completely convinced by the celestial exalted (solar, lunar and sidereal, abyssal) due to the high scale of power they wield, so we decided that in the canon of our campaign these They wouldn't exist. which has not been a problem except for 2 important hooks, the northern bull and the silver pact, the first is important because the destruction of the legions of the house tepet is an important event for the kingdom which is difficult ignore omit plus it shapes much of the setting in the north and the silver pact provides an adversary strong enough to block the kingdom's expansion.<br /> Can anyone give me any suggestions to replace these parts of the canon?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28379,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28379-jose7057","user":"Jose7057","date":". 04-03-2024, 11:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28379-jose7057","name":"Jose7057","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-04T03:53:02-07:00","id":1533555,"title":"","content":"Celestial exalted may still be a myth with no reality (the glorious dragon-blooded revolution was successful beyond all hopes).<br /> The bull and the so-called free solar exaltation may be fair folks using this myth and wrecking havoc or it may have been a breach to malfeas that let a legion of demons pass through. Their leader was a 2nd or 3rd circle demon with bull features and at the end the valiant sacrifice of tepet legions let dragon-blooded sorcerers seal the portal.<br /> The so-called abyssals are just powerful ghosts serving the deathlords and their appearance was tailored to evoke the myths of the mad solars (you can say the same with infernals and shapesifting demons)<br /> The sidereals are not known in the first place, so no big deal<br /> The silver pact is just a convenient excuse for the failures of bad straps: &quot;i couldn't do anything, it's all because big bad shapeshifters. They can be anyone, how was I suppose to know my second-in-command would try to kill me?&quot;<br /> <br /> Or, anything I told you is a lie the imperial administration keeps telling to make you feel safe. Maybe there are still a dozen solars out there looking for revenge against the &quot;usurpers&quot;. Maybe there are dangerous shapeshifters playing the long game and trying to sabotage the realm. If the jade prison was never broken, you may never meet a solar in your life and the border of civilized lands is vast even with 400 lunars that keep to the periphery. Again you may never encounter one.<br /> <br /> Another option is the existence of one or several rival dragon-blooded empires. A know northern empire may have been the cause of the battle of futile blood and the silver pact may be an &quot;secret&quot; alliance of dragon-blooded lands that resist colonization.<br /> <br /> It all depends on how much you want to modify the setting.<br /> The easiest way is leaving the setting as it is (with the jade prison intact) and never meeting a celestial.<br /> The next is saying the important events where cause by gods, demons, fair folks or deathlords (or some combination or alliance) pretending to be celestial (it can even become a plot point)<br /> The hardest way is replacing celestial threats by terrestrial ones: it is the hardest because it requires you to write kingdoms or empires instead of powerful individuals","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1643-maskedfirefly","name":"MaskedFirefly","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-04T19:44:50-07:00","id":1533587,"title":"","content":"I strongly agree with making the Fair Folk your main antagonists and replace the lunars with Fair Folk sympathizers who have been empowered by them using foul magics. Or even corrupted Dragon Bloods of some sort to explain the &quot;Anathema.&quot; I would suggest the Bull of the North is a Dragonblood who has unearthed ancient secrets of the 1st Age, or even an alternate reality (that is a thing in 3e) or even Demonic/Malfean contracts. In 1e/2e there was an artifact that let a Dragonblood summon 2nd circle demons (Mnemon's Emerald Thurible, look up Aspect book: Earth from 1e), which the Bull of the North canonically in 1e/2e had supporters who could do that.<br /> <br /> There are lots of ways to explain away the two plot points. Remember, there are NO RPG POLICE who will bang your door down and arrest you and your friends for BAD WRONG FUN. So long as your group is cool with no Celestial Exalted (maybe they were all killed at the end of the 1st Age, but not before wrecking everything) or maybe they're still all in the Jade Prison. Make something up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2783,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2783-tytalus","user":"Tytalus","date":". 04-04-2024, 10:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2783-tytalus","name":"Tytalus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2783_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"491"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-10T01:00:03-07:00","id":1533940,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the recommendations, I have considered changing Toro del Norte for a group of sorcerers with the support of Octavian and intensifying the presence of fair folk on the edges of creation, your comments have been very helpful, I have also had problems to explain the ruins of the first age but that will be easier, thank you very much","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28379-jose7057","name":"Jose7057","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-10T21:44:34-07:00","id":1534012,"title":"","content":"You're very welcome, and good luck with your game, sounds like it will be lots of fun!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2783-tytalus","name":"Tytalus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2783_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"491"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}